        "id": 1060151
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-15T19:03:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Is there a way to avoid all of the network agent !\u003d null checks? ISTM that if a DataConnection loses control of its network agent, it should take the actions for \"disconnect\" and then stop processing further messages?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1955,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 1955,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "94d773bce23eabca67a3ebe21eb3d2fba4ae43b2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ade8023c_1338fa25",
        "filename": "src/java/com/android/internal/telephony/dataconnection/DataConnection.java",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1955,
      "author": {
        "id": 1081638
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-03-28T00:42:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "It\u0027s extremely hard to support this nicely. The agent is transferred at the time new data connection is established in the other transport. After that we gracefully disconnect the original data connection. But during the time of tearing down this data connection, we needs to be careful not touching anything in the original agent, which has been transferred to the new data connection. Adding a \u0027been-transferred\u0027 flag is as bad as NPE check. The other way to do is overriding all network agent\u0027s methods and checking ownership inside the overridden methods.",
      "parentUuid": "bed74513_b3b59dcb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1955,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 1955,
        "endChar": 37
      },
      "revId": "94d773bce23eabca67a3ebe21eb3d2fba4ae43b2",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": false
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6fb822cb_f940699a",
